<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_VoiceReview"
                  targetNamespace="http://folio-assistant.dev/bpmn/review">

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Voice overlay review — a SUBPROCESS of Process_NarrativeReview.

       Issue #208 asks for the voice review to be part of the "one voice"
       review rather than beside it, and this is where that lands: the
       narrative reviewer descends here after adjudicating the base house
       voice, and takes on no new role — the same `narrative-reviewer` lane
       owns both halves, because a voice is a REGISTER and register is what
       that lane already judges.

       THE FIRST GATEWAY IS THE POINT. A folio that has activated no voice
       must leave immediately, and this diagram says so structurally rather
       than leaving it to a reviewer's discretion. Issue #208: "we shouldnt
       autmoatically apply voices … the folio-asst's own docuemtnation conent
       doesnt have any voice". An unasked-for voice produces confident
       findings against prose that was never written to it.

       THE LOOP OVER VOICES IS SEQUENTIAL AND DELIBERATE. Rules from several
       active voices are UNIONED, not merged, so two voices may both speak
       about capitalisation and both findings stand. A reviewer reading a
       finding has to know which voice raised it, and a merged pass would
       lose that.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:process id="Process_VoiceReview" name="Voice overlay review" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The voice axis: load whichever editorial voices are active, run each rule's mechanical half, and decide — for each finding — whether the prose is wrong, the rule does not apply to this content, or this block is a stated exception.

You are in this process after the base voice has been adjudicated, and only if a voice is active at all: the first gateway ends the process honestly when none is, rather than reporting a clean review of nothing.

Three outcomes, all legitimate, and the third is the one that needs recording: an exception without a reviewer entry is indistinguishable from a rule nobody ran. There is also a fourth path the diagram draws deliberately — if the rule's own citation does not support it, the RULE is the defect, and that becomes a bean rather than a finding against the prose.</bpmn:documentation>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_VoiceReview">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_NarrativeReviewer" name="Narrative reviewer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs every active voice to completion rather than stopping at the first, because rules from separate voices are UNIONED rather than merged — two voices can both flag capitalisation and both findings must stand, so folding voice N+1's pass into voice N's would lose which voice raised what. At each citation, this lane also has to route the defect to the right place: a rule its own citation does not support goes to Task_RuleIsWrong as a finding against the VOICE, never into Task_Adjudicate, which only ever judges the block.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_BaseVoiceDone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_AnyActive</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_NoVoice</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_LoadActive</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_MechanicalHalf</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_OpenCitation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_QuoteSupports</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RuleIsWrong</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Adjudicate</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_MoreVoices</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RecordOnSidecar</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_VoiceReviewed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_BaseVoiceDone" name="Base voice&#10;adjudicated"/>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_AnyActive" name="Any voice&#10;activated?"/>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_NoVoice" name="No voice —&#10;nothing to review">
      <bpmn:documentation>A pass, not a gap. An empty `voices.active` is the default and a legitimate answer: this instance ships four voices and activates none.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_LoadActive" name="Load the active voices">
      <bpmn:documentation>The activated set only, never everything shipped. An id naming no shipped voice is an error rather than a skip — a folio that believes it is applying a voice and is applying nothing has the cleanest-looking output of the three.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_MechanicalHalf" name="Run the rule's mechanical half">
      <bpmn:documentation>Whatever `patterns` and `terminology` the rule carries. A `judgementOnly` rule has no mechanical half by declaration, which is different from nobody having written one yet.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_OpenCitation" name="Open the rule's citation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every rule resolves to a real `library/` section or a KG node, and carries the quote it was read from. Opening it is what lets a reviewer say WHY the rule applies — and it is the only way to catch a rule that misread its own source.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_QuoteSupports" name="Does the quote&#10;support the rule?"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RuleIsWrong" name="The RULE is the defect — bean it">
      <bpmn:documentation>A rule its own quote does not support is a finding against the voice, not against the block. Measured precedent: `voice-editorializing` flags "clearly", and the exemplar the Milnor gate is named after uses it fourteen times as proof economy (bean `2t41`).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/>
        <folio:bean op="note"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Adjudicate" calledElement="Process_Adjudication" name="Adjudicate: prose, scope, or exception">
      <bpmn:documentation>The same three outcomes as the base voice axis. The register is wrong for this block (fix the prose); the rule does not apply to this content (scope it on the voice, one edit rather than ten overrules); or the rule applies and this block is an exception (a reviewer entry saying why).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/><folio:skill ref="adjudication"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:callActivity>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_MoreVoices" name="Another active&#10;voice?"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RecordOnSidecar" name="Record on the block's QA sidecar">
      <bpmn:documentation>Through `qa-merge-findings`, so the icon and the published witness agree with the decision. The adjudication LEADS the criterion and the script entry is kept beneath it: a disagreement between a checker and a reviewer is information.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="voice-overlay-review"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_VoiceReviewed" name="Voices&#10;adjudicated"/>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V1" sourceRef="Start_BaseVoiceDone" targetRef="GW_AnyActive"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V2" name="none" sourceRef="GW_AnyActive" targetRef="End_NoVoice"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V3" name="one or more" sourceRef="GW_AnyActive" targetRef="Task_LoadActive"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V4" sourceRef="Task_LoadActive" targetRef="Task_MechanicalHalf"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V5" sourceRef="Task_MechanicalHalf" targetRef="Task_OpenCitation"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V6" sourceRef="Task_OpenCitation" targetRef="GW_QuoteSupports"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V7" name="no" sourceRef="GW_QuoteSupports" targetRef="Task_RuleIsWrong"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V8" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_QuoteSupports" targetRef="Task_Adjudicate"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V9" sourceRef="Task_RuleIsWrong" targetRef="GW_MoreVoices"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V10" sourceRef="Task_Adjudicate" targetRef="GW_MoreVoices"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V11" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_MoreVoices" targetRef="Task_MechanicalHalf"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V12" name="no" sourceRef="GW_MoreVoices" targetRef="Task_RecordOnSidecar"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_V13" sourceRef="Task_RecordOnSidecar" targetRef="End_VoiceReviewed"/>

  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_VoiceReview">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_VoiceReview" bpmnElement="Process_VoiceReview">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Lane_NarrativeReviewer_V" bpmnElement="Lane_NarrativeReviewer" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1560" height="360"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Start_BaseVoiceDone" bpmnElement="Start_BaseVoiceDone">
        <dc:Bounds x="200" y="212" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_AnyActive" bpmnElement="GW_AnyActive" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="280" y="205" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_NoVoice" bpmnElement="End_NoVoice">
        <dc:Bounds x="287" y="120" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_LoadActive" bpmnElement="Task_LoadActive">
        <dc:Bounds x="380" y="190" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_MechanicalHalf" bpmnElement="Task_MechanicalHalf">
        <dc:Bounds x="570" y="190" width="160" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_OpenCitation" bpmnElement="Task_OpenCitation">
        <dc:Bounds x="770" y="190" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_QuoteSupports" bpmnElement="GW_QuoteSupports" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="960" y="205" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_RuleIsWrong" bpmnElement="Task_RuleIsWrong">
        <dc:Bounds x="1050" y="100" width="170" height="70"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_Adjudicate" bpmnElement="Task_Adjudicate">
        <dc:Bounds x="1050" y="290" width="170" height="70"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_MoreVoices" bpmnElement="GW_MoreVoices" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1270" y="205" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_RecordOnSidecar" bpmnElement="Task_RecordOnSidecar">
        <dc:Bounds x="1370" y="190" width="170" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_VoiceReviewed" bpmnElement="End_VoiceReviewed">
        <dc:Bounds x="1600" y="212" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V1" bpmnElement="F_V1">
        <di:waypoint x="236" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="280" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V2" bpmnElement="F_V2">
        <di:waypoint x="305" y="205"/><di:waypoint x="305" y="156"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V3" bpmnElement="F_V3">
        <di:waypoint x="330" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="380" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V4" bpmnElement="F_V4">
        <di:waypoint x="530" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="570" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V5" bpmnElement="F_V5">
        <di:waypoint x="730" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="770" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V6" bpmnElement="F_V6">
        <di:waypoint x="920" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="960" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V7" bpmnElement="F_V7">
        <di:waypoint x="985" y="205"/><di:waypoint x="985" y="135"/><di:waypoint x="1050" y="135"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V8" bpmnElement="F_V8">
        <di:waypoint x="985" y="255"/><di:waypoint x="985" y="325"/><di:waypoint x="1050" y="325"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V9" bpmnElement="F_V9">
        <di:waypoint x="1220" y="135"/><di:waypoint x="1295" y="135"/><di:waypoint x="1295" y="205"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V10" bpmnElement="F_V10">
        <di:waypoint x="1220" y="325"/><di:waypoint x="1295" y="325"/><di:waypoint x="1295" y="255"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V11" bpmnElement="F_V11">
        <di:waypoint x="1295" y="205"/><di:waypoint x="1295" y="410"/><di:waypoint x="650" y="410"/><di:waypoint x="650" y="270"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V12" bpmnElement="F_V12">
        <di:waypoint x="1320" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="1370" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_V13" bpmnElement="F_V13">
        <di:waypoint x="1540" y="230"/><di:waypoint x="1600" y="230"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
